&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.320
The theory of quantum mechanics developed from a&nbsp;
set of mysteries in the late 1800s and early 1900s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.160
where reality didn’t quite match&nbsp;
the models of physics at the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.920
We now call these older theories of physics,&nbsp;
classical physics. There were several clues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:48.320
that pointed to some deeper model of reality.
When light shines through a gas, the gas absorbs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:54.080
and emits specific frequencies of light which we&nbsp;
call atomic spectra. This was a mystery there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.120
no known classical explanation for this.
And there was a lot of confusion about how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.440
atoms could be stable. In classical physics&nbsp;
the electrons should continually radiate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.320
their energy and collapse into the nucleus.
The source of radioactivity was unknown.
&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.360
When you look at a hot body like the Sun,&nbsp;
it emits electromagnetic radiation in many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.440
different frequencies and this distribution&nbsp;
of light is called blackbody radiation. 
&nbsp;

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.120
Now the distribution we observe&nbsp;
from black bodies didn’t match&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.760
the predictions of classical physics.
And when you shine light on certain metals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.720
you can make electrons fly off, this is&nbsp;
called the photoelectric effect. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.760
experiment showed that light didn’t behave like&nbsp;
a wave, but like a stream of particles and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.154
the first indication of particle wave duality.
All of these mysteries can only be explained with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.154 --> 00:02:40.240
the laws of quantum mechanics.
Let’s take a look at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.000
foundations of quantum mechanics.
A cornerstone experiment in quantum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.520
mechanics is the double slit experiment where&nbsp;
electrons are fired through two thin slits and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:55.200
make an interference pattern on a detector behind.&nbsp;
This interference pattern is something you only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.480
see with waves and this is more experimental&nbsp;
evidence for particle wave-duality.
&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.520
In actual fact, in the mathematics of quantum&nbsp;
mechanics all particles are described as waves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.720
by a thing called a wavefunction, and the way this&nbsp;
wave evolves over time is described by the famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:17.840
Shrodinger equation. But we can never see these&nbsp;
quantum waves as all we ever detect are particles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.480
but from the wave function we can predict&nbsp;
where the particles are likely to turn up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.840
but we have to do a bit of maths&nbsp;
on them first called the Born rule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:31.840
which derives a probability distribution of where&nbsp;
the particle might be from the wavefunction.
&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.560
So quantum mechanics tells us that the universe is&nbsp;
fundamentally probabilistic, we don’t know exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:45.200
where the particle will turn up the best we have&nbsp;
is a probability of where it will be. This brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.840
us to the Heisenberg uncertainty principle&nbsp;
which says that quantum objects don’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:55.520
definite values for certain pairs of properties,&nbsp;
for example, position and momentum. You can get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.320
a flavour of this from these pictures. The first&nbsp;
is a snapshot where the particle had a definite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.200
position, but we have no information about its&nbsp;
momentum, as in: the direction it was going and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:11.920
how fast it was travelling. The second picture has&nbsp;
a motion blur which tells us about its momentum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.640
but now we have got an uncertainty about where&nbsp;
the particle was when we took the picture. 
&nbsp;

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:23.040
Another important equation is the Dirac&nbsp;
equation which extends the Schrodinger equation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.720
to include special relativity and describe&nbsp;
particles with high kinetic energy. And another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:33.920
important foundational concept is Bell’s theorem&nbsp;
which proved that the uncertainty in quantum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:40.080
mechanics is not caused by our lack of knowledge&nbsp;
about hidden variables, but is a fundamental part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.200
of the universe, and also led to the concept of&nbsp;
non-locality which we’ll meet a little later.
&nbsp;

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.880
Finally we get to energy quantization&nbsp;
which is where objects like electrons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.080
can only have certain definite energies when&nbsp;
they are in atoms. This is where the quantum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.080
in quantum mechanics comes from. And this&nbsp;
quantization is because their wave functions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.920
can only vibrate in certain specific ways.
You can see this if I reduce the atom to one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.840
dimension. The energy field of the proton in&nbsp;
the atom is represented by this bucket shape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.720
you can think of the electron as being attracted&nbsp;
to the proton and so it wants to fall into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:22.720
bottom of the bucket. But because the electron&nbsp;
is a wave it can only exist in certain modes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.160
shown here which are just like the vibrational&nbsp;
modes of a guitar string, with higher frequency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.680
modes having a higher energy.
This also means that the quantum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.320
objects always have a minimum amount of&nbsp;
energy known as the zero-point energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:42.320
and this applies not only to electrons in atoms,&nbsp;
but to everything, even to empty space itself.
